   196	# --- three states for every path this trainer asks about (close reviews 14, 15) ------
   197	# ``Path.is_file()`` answers False both for a path that is not there and for one it
   198	# could not inspect: a self-referential ``<attempt>.resolved`` raises ELOOP inside it and
   199	# comes back "no tombstone", so a trainer whose launch had been retired registered
   200	# anyway. Nothing here decides on ``is_file``. The classification is the launcher's --
   201	# literally: the same tools/exp11_pathprobe.py, where the errno is available.
   202	PRESENT = exp11_pathprobe.PRESENT
   203	ABSENT = exp11_pathprobe.ABSENT
   204	UNSURE = exp11_pathprobe.UNKNOWN
   205	probe_path = exp11_pathprobe.probe
   206	file_state = exp11_pathprobe.file_state
